(>> 5.5 Event Propagation: Bubbling, Capturing & Event Delegation) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(When an event occurs on a nested child element, it propagates through three sequential) Tj
T*
(phases:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Capturing \(Trickling\) Phase: Event travels down from window -> document -> body) Tj
T*
(-> parent to the target element.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Target Phase: Event fires on the target element itself.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Bubbling Phase: Event bubbles upward from target -> parent -> body -> document) Tj
T*
(-> window.) Tj
T*
(* Event Control Methods: event.stopPropagation\(\) \(halts upward bubbling\),) Tj
T*
(event.preventDefault\(\) \(cancels default browser action, e.g. prevents form submission) Tj
T*
(or link following\).) Tj
T*
(* Event Delegation Pattern: Performance optimization where a single event listener is) Tj
T*
(attached to a common parent element rather than attaching hundreds of individual) Tj
T*
(listeners to child elements. Uses event.target to identify which child triggered the) Tj
T*
(event.) Tj
