(>> 5.6 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Explain Event Bubbling and Event Capturing in the DOM event flow, detailing how) Tj
T*
(Event Delegation exploits this architecture.) Tj
T*
(Answer: When an event occurs on a target DOM element, browser event propagation executes) Tj
T*
(in three phases: \(1\) Capturing phase: the event trickles down from the window, document,) Tj
T*
(and ancestor nodes down to the target. \(2\) Target phase: the event triggers on the) Tj
T*
(element itself. \(3\) Bubbling phase: the event bubbles upward through parent ancestors) Tj
T*
(back to window. Event Delegation is a high-performance design pattern that leverages) Tj
T*
(bubbling: instead of binding hundreds of event listeners to individual child elements) Tj
T*
(\(e.g. <li> items in a large list\), a single listener is placed on the parent container) Tj
T*
(\(<ul>\). When any child is clicked, the event bubbles up to the parent; the parent) Tj
T*
(handler checks event.target to process the action, drastically reducing memory usage and) Tj
T*
(automatically supporting dynamically injected child elements.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Differentiate between 'textContent', 'innerText', and 'innerHTML' in DOM) Tj
T*
(scripting, highlighting security considerations regarding XSS attacks.) Tj
T*
(Answer: 'textContent' retrieves or sets raw text content of a node and all descendants,) Tj
T*
(including hidden text \(<script>, <style>\), without parsing HTML markup. 'innerText') Tj
T*
(returns rendered visible text, taking CSS styling and layout into account \(e.g. ignores) Tj
T*
(text hidden by display: none\). 'innerHTML' retrieves or sets raw HTML markup inside an) Tj
T*
(element, instructing the browser engine to parse strings into DOM elements. Security) Tj
T*
(Concern: Using 'innerHTML' with untrusted user-supplied input creates severe Cross-Site) Tj
T*
(Scripting \(XSS\) vulnerabilities, enabling attackers to inject malicious <script> tags or) Tj
T*
(<img onerror='...'> payloads to steal cookies and session tokens. Safe applications use) Tj
T*
('textContent' or dedicated DOM construction methods.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.7 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
